.spec/security-privacy.md-33-## Client credentials
.spec/security-privacy.md-34-
.spec/security-privacy.md-35-- Private keys and passphrases live in the Data Protection Keychain and are
.spec/security-privacy.md-36-  shared only through the minimum keychain access group required by the app and
.spec/security-privacy.md-37-  its packet tunnel extension.
.spec/security-privacy.md-38-- App Group storage contains non-secret profile configuration and opaque Keychain
.spec/security-privacy.md-39-  references, never raw private keys or passphrases.
.spec/security-privacy.md:40:- Key import validates format and permissions. Key generation uses platform
.spec/security-privacy.md-41-  cryptography and never exports silently.
.spec/security-privacy.md-42-- Secrets are not placed in `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration`,
.spec/security-privacy.md-43-  logs, crash annotations, shell commands, or task-board resources.
.spec/security-privacy.md-44-- Agent forwarding is disabled.
.spec/security-privacy.md-45-
.spec/security-privacy.md-46-## Relay supply chain
.spec/security-privacy.md-47-
.spec/security-privacy.md-48-- Relay assets are built from pinned source revisions in CI for the declared
.spec/security-privacy.md-49-  OS/architecture matrix.
.spec/security-privacy.md-50-- The application bundle contains a manifest with protocol version, platform,
.spec/security-privacy.md-51-  file size, and SHA-256 for every asset.
.spec/security-privacy.md-52-- Upload occurs only after SSH host verification and authentication.
.spec/security-privacy.md:53:- Remote installation uses private permissions, checksum verification, and
.spec/security-privacy.md-54-  atomic rename; a mismatch never executes.
.spec/security-privacy.md-55-- The relay performs a versioned handshake and reports its build identity.
.spec/security-privacy.md-56-- Third-party notices for HEV, hev-task-system, hev-socks5-core, lwIP, the SSH
.spec/security-privacy.md-57-  engine, and any relay dependency ship with the product.
.spec/security-privacy.md-58-
.spec/security-privacy.md-59-## Traffic and routing safety
.spec/security-privacy.md-60-
.spec/security-privacy.md-61-- Ordinary traffic and DNS fail closed on mandatory tunnel failure.
