LOGBOOK.md-21-- CONFORMANCE: A live OpenSSH fixture now authenticates an in-memory Ed25519 credential through the adapter's async `SSHPublicKeyCredential.sign` callback, records an actual opaque-signer invocation, preserves host-policy-before-credential ordering, carries only a Keychain-shaped credential reference, runs exec, and returns every owned resource to zero. The existing P-256 deployed-fallback coverage remains intact.
