LOGBOOK.md-232-- ROOT CAUSE: r3 granted `com.apple.security.application-groups` on both macOS production targets with the purpose *"the sandbox-visible shared namespace for the host↔provider channel selected by `TASK-260728-7ii1xz` **will** use"*, plus "so C1 need not be repeated". Reviewer verdict 03 blocked it: a possible future transport plus an operational convenience are not a current requirement. Both halves confirmed against the r3 artifact. The generalisable failure is **holding a capability open against an undecided design** — it reads as prudent and is indistinguishable from over-provisioning until the design lands.
