LOGBOOK.md-234-- FINDING: What the entitlement grants on macOS is readable, not arguable. `/System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb` (26.5/25F71) contains exactly two `sandbox-array-entitlement` blocks for the key — lines **302-330** and **459-465** — conferring six grants. Three are **home-relative** and therefore break across the root/user split (group container r/w; `network-bind`/`network-outbound` inside it; `~/Library/Application Scripts/<suite>`). Three are **system-wide and do work across it**: `/Library/Application Support/AppStore/GroupContent/<suite>`, `mach-lookup`/`mach-register` on `global-name-prefix "<suite>."` (**lines 326-328** — the XPC channel, and the only reason the macOS group ever looked load-bearing), and `ipc-posix*` on `ipc-posix-name-prefix "<suite>/"` (**line 329** — POSIX shm, which no candidate ever proposed). "App Groups do nothing on macOS" would be the tidy version and it is false; the verdict rests on *these grants are unused*, not on *the entitlement is inert*.
