 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2255 — Owner selects resumed functional evidence for Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta)
+- OWNER DECISION: Option B from reviewer verdict 01 is accepted. ADR-028 and the C1 contract now distinguish one human-input board node from one continuous human sitting; the resumed 2026-07-28/2026-08-10 interactions remain one ceremony node, with the intervening producer/reviewer cycle stated rather than concealed.
+- EVIDENCE POLICY: Effective prompt-free signing through the named identities/tools and authenticated Relux Works portal/team authority replace retrospective proof of the historical Always Allow click and separately timestamped two-factor completion. Missing interaction boundaries remain missing; no uninterrupted-session claim is allowed.
+- PRIVACY POLICY: Credential values and secret paths remain prohibited in repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history. Safe command-name-only history does not fail the ceremony; secret-bearing arguments, credential input, identifiers, account credentials, and key bytes still do.
+
+### 2234 — Ceremony C1 review stops on non-retroactive human evidence (TASK-260728-q5kjta)
+- REVIEW VERDICT: BLOCKED. The privacy-safe record is honest, the r12 matrix and live-consumer gates pass, and the targeted leak scan is clean, but the record itself says the ceremony resumed across 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-10 with producer/reviewer work between interactions and without captured interaction start/end times. That directly fails literal AC1.
+- EVIDENCE GAPS: Prompt-free `/usr/bin/codesign` probes demonstrate effective access but cannot prove the required Always Allow grants were performed in C1; an authenticated portal session does not prove two-factor completed during C1; two safe credential command-name lines in history mean literal per-command history suppression cannot be claimed. These facts cannot be repaired retrospectively by editing the outcome.
+- RESOLUTION: Recommended path is one newly timed, uninterrupted owner sitting that idempotently repeats/confirms every in-scope grant, captures privacy-safe contemporaneous facts, and runs with history/echo suppression. Alternative is an explicit owner architecture/product decision to amend AC1/AC2/AC3/AC7 and ADR-028 to accept resumed functional evidence; accepting the current record under the unchanged contract is not valid.
+
+### 2228 — Ceremony C1 resumed honestly under the accepted r12 macOS-only authority (TASK-260728-q5kjta)
+- DEVIATION: C1 began on 2026-07-28 and owner confirmation resumed on 2026-08-10; exact human-interaction start/end times were not captured, and producer/reviewer work occurred between the interactions. The record must not claim one uninterrupted sitting or literal AC1 timing compliance.
+- AUTHORITY: The owner confirmed an authenticated Apple Developer session for Relux Works, LLC and authority for revision `2026-07-28.r12`: exactly the four macOS App IDs, Network Extensions on all four, and one Mac Development profile per App ID with this Apple-silicon Mac registered. No App Group record/capability, Keychain access-group portal mutation, iOS App ID, distribution profile, or `works.relux.proxy` change is authorized.
+- CUSTODY: Prompt-free `/usr/bin/codesign` probes succeeded for the named Apple Development and Developer ID Application identities; the named `relux-works-notary` profile is in the login Keychain; the owner retained the source notarization private-key file as owner-controlled recovery material outside repo/board/logs; Sparkle 2.9.4 generated the EdDSA private key into login-Keychain custody.
+- PRIVACY: Targeted post-ceremony scans found zero secret/key-path/key-ID/issuer-ID/account-credential candidate files in the Git-scoped repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history, and zero key files in repository/board scope. History nevertheless contains one safe Sparkle generation command-name line and one safe Keychain-unlock command-name line, with no password flags; full history suppression therefore cannot be claimed.
+- ANOMALY: The older `TASK-260728-3a2dnr_ceremony-c1.md` planning artifact predates matrix rule G4/K2 and still describes two macOS IDs plus App Group/Keychain grants. It is historical and must not drive execution; the live task contract and accepted r12 matrix are authoritative.
+
 ### 2207 — libssh2 live evidence closes Ed25519 and automatic-rekey review gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
 - CONFORMANCE: A live OpenSSH fixture now authenticates an in-memory Ed25519 credential through the adapter's async `SSHPublicKeyCredential.sign` callback, records an actual opaque-signer invocation, preserves host-policy-before-credential ordering, carries only a Keychain-shaped credential reference, runs exec, and returns every owned resource to zero. The existing P-256 deployed-fallback coverage remains intact.
 - CONFORMANCE: Deterministic byte-threshold and injected-clock time-threshold tests drive the production libssh2 KEX path with an open channel, assert typed trigger/success events and `clientByteRekeys`/`clientTimeRekeys`, prove post-KEX traffic, and restore sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, allocations, and buffers to baseline after cancel/close.

