dy grants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No value, no portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change. FIELD-BY-FIELD (all five keys on the row): status prohibited-pending-decision -> prohibited; rationale -> the settled reason above citing TASK-260728-7ii1xz; evidence -> keep and add application.sb:792-793 plus checks E8-E10; resolutionOwner -> REMOVE (this task IS the resolution; a settled row naming a pending resolver reads as still-open); amendmentRule -> REMOVE and replace with M5. The amendmentRule removal is the critical one: its antecedent (transport gives the provider direct keychain access) is now TRUE while its consequent (amend to required with the group literal) is FALSE, so left in place it is a live instruction to re-grant the row on exactly the reasoning this decision refutes. M2: close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz as resolver. M3: keep OC-4 open, downgraded to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected. M4: macos.host keychain-access-groups - no change requested, recommend keep granted with the purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus a macOS pre-seed staging item. M5: record the replacement rule - on macOS the file-based keychain is SecAccess-ACL controlled and keychain-access-groups applies only to the Data Protection Keychain, so a root-context provider never needs it and the presence of the key in a shipping third-party provider is not evidence it functions; the row reopens only if the provider is ever moved into a user context. M6: application-groups on both macOS targets - no value change, but the stated purpose and the section 10 traceability row implying a shared container on macOS are FALSE (host and provider resolve different containers). M7: bump revision, append a revisionLog entry naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz_reviewer-verdict-01.md and this decision, keep validate-matrix at exit 0, and check that deleting resolutionOwner/amendmentRule does not trip an exhaustive containment assertion - if one requires them it encoded the open state and must be updated in the same revision. Consider a negative gate: a prohibited row still carrying a resolutionOwner is a contradiction. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d)\nr4 rework against reviewer verdict 03 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1 plus a secondary correction), and application of the TASK-260728-7ii1xz r2 amendment packet M1-M7 in the same revision because M1 and F1 touch the same two rows. F1 independently CONFIRMED against the r3 artifact. Neither of the reviewer two exits applied verbatim: 7ii1xz finished in the interim and its M6 explicitly handed the least-privilege call to this task, so the survey was done rather than the row deferred again. Verdict: com.apple.security.application-groups is PROHIBITED on all four macOS targets (production AND probe) and required on all four iOS targets - new rule G4. Basis is a grant-by-grant read of /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb 26.5/25F71 at lines 302-330 and 459-465, the only two places the key appears: six grants, three home-relative and broken across the root/user split, three system-wide and belonging to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service which 7ii1xz rejected as candidate C, group-prefixed POSIX IPC which nobody proposed). 