ion, assertion scope or C1 mutation set changed. Board footprint: one dependency edge added, and one field on one element - TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope, revision label r8 to r9, character delta 0, verified byte-exact, required by amendmentRule. No board element created, deleted, re-parented or re-scoped; no portal mutation; no product source, spec file or generated project touched. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-ae0e2a, pid=3124, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-83cf4c)\nReviewer verdict 08 (2026-07-28): CHANGES REQUESTED, route analysis. Blocking F1: the matrix permanently omits a /Library/Keychains sandbox file exception using only macOS 26.5 application.sb evidence, while the binding generated-target floor is macOS 15.0. No OS-version constraint or reopening rule covers sandbox-policy drift, so automated allowlists could reject an entitlement required on a supported floor. Verify the grant and securityd lookups on macOS 15/oldest supported runtime or model the version-specific uncertainty, extend K1/X1 and negative gates, and attach durable r8 input if preserve.py remains claimed. Evidence: TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-08.md. Independent exits: validator 0 (2483), mutations 0 (202/202), board consumer 0 (84), reviewer gates 0, legacy 0, board validate 0, swift test 0 (335/29). preserve.py not rerun because r8 input is not attached.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nsp