 ## 2026-08-10
 
+### 2255 — Owner selects resumed functional evidence for Ceremony C1 (TASK-260728-q5kjta)
+- OWNER DECISION: Option B from reviewer verdict 01 is accepted. ADR-028 and the C1 contract now distinguish one human-input board node from one continuous human sitting; the resumed 2026-07-28/2026-08-10 interactions remain one ceremony node, with the intervening producer/reviewer cycle stated rather than concealed.
+- EVIDENCE POLICY: Effective prompt-free signing through the named identities/tools and authenticated Relux Works portal/team authority replace retrospective proof of the historical Always Allow click and separately timestamped two-factor completion. Missing interaction boundaries remain missing; no uninterrupted-session claim is allowed.
+- PRIVACY POLICY: Credential values and secret paths remain prohibited in repository, board resources, run logs, and shell history. Safe command-name-only history does not fail the ceremony; secret-bearing arguments, credential input, identifiers, account credentials, and key bytes still do.
+
 ### 2234 — Ceremony C1 review stops on non-retroactive human evidence (TASK-260728-q5kjta)
 - REVIEW VERDICT: BLOCKED. The privacy-safe record is honest, the r12 matrix and live-consumer gates pass, and the targeted leak scan is clean, but the record itself says the ceremony resumed across 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-10 with producer/reviewer work between interactions and without captured interaction start/end times. That directly fails literal AC1.
 - EVIDENCE GAPS: Prompt-free `/usr/bin/codesign` probes demonstrate effective access but cannot prove the required Always Allow grants were performed in C1; an authenticated portal session does not prove two-factor completed during C1; two safe credential command-name lines in history mean literal per-command history suppression cannot be claimed. These facts cannot be repaired retrospectively by editing the outcome.

